@cjlarose I was thinking about this yesterday I don't think the problem lies with the `CheckPending` migrations middleware. The root cause of the problem for your case is that any mutex around `ActiveRecord::Base.connection` will cause the problem because checking out a connection may result in an autoload. A mutex around `ActiveRecord::Base.connection` can happen in the framework code or in another library so I don't think this is a bug in the framework at the moment. 

I'm not that familiar with code reloading in Rails but something from the [docs for the classic autoloader](https://guides.rubyonrails.org/threading_and_code_execution.html#permit-concurrent-loads) stood out  

> Other blocking operations performed inside the Executor block (which includes all application code), however, can needlessly retain the running lock. If another thread encounters a constant it must autoload, this can cause a deadlock.
